lines+=['## Walls, spans, landings and module boundaries','','- Every inspected Court arcade foot, rest alcove, bench foot, Bath circular gateway, divider wing and rounded divider meets actual deck geometry. Top Court arcade faces meet named ArcadeRoofConnection objects; Bath gateway top meets roof at 5.200 m.','- Inner dado/plaster bedding meets the level below. Headers, roof slabs and barrel surfaces intentionally span openings. An overhead downward ray that reaches a floor metres below is diagnostic distance, not automatically an unsupported-beam failure. Side/end engagement and the exact section must be considered.','- Basin stairs retain four 0.500 m treads, five equal 0.148 m rises from -0.220 to +0.520 m. All stair bases bed into solid basin floor. Entry stairs retain 0.500 m treads and 0.155 m rises, first top +0.365 m, final step -0.565 m, adjoining common floor -0.720 m.','- The 0.300 m outboard half of each North/West shared wall lies beyond the standalone source foundation boundary ±16 m. It has no local receiver in an isolated .blend. A separate ray test translates the actual CommonFoundation mesh into the north/west 32 m neighboring cell: all these rays then meet the translated solid at -0.720 m.','- Static runtime source agrees with that shared-cell contract: pool_world.gd creates neighboring shells on a 32 m grid; ordinary room_builder.gd uses ContinuousBasinFloor top -0.720 m; expanded modules use the same floor datum. This is static geometry/code evidence. Native instance presence/loading and gameplay should be checked separately by the runtime QA. No claim is made that this worker observed those native neighbors.','','## Normals, UVs, transforms and export preservation','','- Every final visible source mesh is closed and manifold, has consistently oriented adjacent faces and positive signed volume. Every source world matrix is identity; assembly coordinates are baked into vertices. No scale/origin offset explains the original floating piers.','- Metric UV edge ratios meet the expected 1 UV unit/metre to float precision. Bath gateway has one preserved diagnostic flag: ratio 1.002057 on a 0.1054 mm edge, absolute mismatch 0.000000217 m. For edges at least 1 cm, ratios are 0.999979–1.000024. Maximum absolute UV/edge metric discrepancy is 0.000000516 m, not perceptible tile stretching.','- Static GLB parser compares every visible triangle against source world-space geometry after 0.1 mm quantization, preserving duplicates. All three match. Every collision box name and transformed bound matches its authored source proxy within 0.01 mm. Court 159, Lanes 165, Bath 196 collision boxes. These are preservation checks, not a replacement for native collision playtesting.','- Ordinary render/proxy box pairs have exactly matching source bounds. Imported curved forms retain their intentional conservative BOX-only collision decomposition. No new trimesh or GPU/import process was used by this audit.','','## Method, evidence and reproducibility','','Actual lower-face triangle centroids plus inset vertices are sampled on the real transformed mesh. Arch/bench feet are reported in separate real foot regions, not the hollow bbox centre. Rays exclude the object itself, COLLISION_ proxy meshes and water-named geometry. Solid BasinBottom meshes remain receivers. Penetration is detected per candidate receiver by downward exit and upward exit normals, so the 10 cm footing embed cannot be mistaken for a 40 cm gap to the basin lower face. Contact tolerance is 2 mm to distinguish imported bevel-edge samples from meaningful construction gaps.','','Sections are exact plane/triangle intersections in Godot X/Y-up/Z coordinates, fixed across before/after. They are source Blender drawings, not native screenshots. Water is only a reference datum. The source .blend SHA256 is checked before and after opening, and no input file is saved.','','Evidence files:','- lanes_contact_comparison.png: fixed-axis pier, roof and entry transition before/after.','- baseline/all_rooms_sections.png and candidate/all_rooms_sections.png: complete three-room section overview.','- retained_boundary_details.png: corrected jamb and shared-cell wall details.','- contact_foot_regions.csv: all target base regions, actual receiver names and signed gaps.','- baseline/*.json, candidate/*.json: exact sample coordinates, receivers, normals, sections, source hashes and mesh metadata.','- baseline/glb_preservation.json, candidate/glb_preservation.json: independent export geometry hashes/collision comparisons.','- intermediate-before-jamb-fix/: prior candidate snapshot preserving the trim-lip finding.','','Commands are documented in tools/architecture_contact_qa/README.md.']
